.Dd July 26, 2026
.Dt UPDATE 8
.Os FreeBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm update
.Nd rebase a workspace onto a new foundation patch level
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl s Ar name
.Op Fl k Ar kind
.Op Fl a Ar artifact
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl q
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility is part of the parasa framework for FreeBSD system management.
It rebases a system or container onto a newer foundation artifact
without destroying the running clone.
.Pp
.Sy Core principle:
never destroy the running clone during update.
The new state is built in a
.Dq -new
clone alongside the live one.
The old box keeps running until the admin verifies the new one works,
then
.Xr finalize_update 8
swaps them.
.Pp
The update proceeds as follows:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Sy Pre-flight:
verify no unsaved drift, check that
.Ao Ar name Ac Ns -new
does not already exist, resolve old and new artifacts.
.It
.Sy Beam down:
incremental ZFS send from old to new artifact, clone into
.Pa {kind}s/ Ns Ao Ar name Ac Ns -new .
.It
.Sy Mount:
start the -new clone with data-lake datasets mounted.
For containers, a temporary jail is started.
For systems, data datasets are mounted and commands run via chroot.
.It
.Sy Recipe replay:
source
.Pa compose.sh ,
call pre_pkg(), install packages from
.Pa pkg.list ,
call post_pkg().
.It
.Sy Git rebase:
replay the entire admin delta chain onto the new artifact commit.
In quiet mode, conflicts cause an immediate abort (old clone untouched).
In interactive mode, the admin resolves conflicts inline.
.It
.Sy Derivation regen:
for each derivation whose source file changed during rebase,
regenerate the binary.
.It
.Sy Validate:
regenerate mtree.dist and run
.Xr diff 8 .
.It
.Sy Offer swap:
stop the -new jail/unmount and print
.Xr finalize_update 8
instructions.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-a ARTIFACT"
.It Fl h
Print a usage summary and exit.
.It Fl d
Dry run.
Show what would be done without making changes.
.It Fl s Ar name
Specify the workspace name.
This option is required.
.It Fl k Ar kind
Specify "system" or "container".
Auto-detected from recipes directory if omitted.
.It Fl a Ar artifact
Specify the target artifact name.
Defaults to the latest snapshot on the foundation archive.
.It Fl q
Quiet mode.
Abort on rebase conflicts instead of prompting.
.El
.Sh ROLLBACK
If the -new clone is bad, simply destroy it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zfs destroy -r zbereshit/{kind}s/<name>-new
.Ed
.Pp
The old clone is never touched during update.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "zbamidbar/foundation.zfs/foundations/<foundation>"
.It Pa zbereshit/{kind}s/ Ns Ao Ar name Ac Ns -new
The new clone built during update.
.It Pa zbamidbar/foundation.zfs/foundations/ Ns Ao Ar foundation Ac
Foundation archive containing snapshots.
.It Pa zbamidbar/foundation.git
Git repository with foundation and workspace branches.
.It Pa recipes/{kind}s/ Ns Ao Ar name Ac Ns Pa /compose.sh
Recipe script with pre_pkg() and post_pkg() functions.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr finalize_update 8 ,
.Xr diff 8 ,
.Xr save 8 ,
.Xr zfs-clone 8 ,
.Xr zfs-send 8
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
utility is part of the parasa framework.
